-housing capital works. Investments were \u00a344.4m (of which \u00a340.2m in money market funds, all maturities under one year) yielding 3.90% against a 3.75% SONIA benchmark, and the s151 officer reports no limit breaches in the quarter and no difficulties envisaged in complying with the prudential indicators.","fy":"2026/27","as_of_doc":"Quarter 1 Review 2026/27: Treasury Management and Annual Investment Strategy","as_of_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s96942/Treasury Q1 26-27 GA - Google Docs.pdf","as_of_date":"2026-07-29","signals":[{"code":"borrowing-increase","headline":"Gross debt \u00a390.5m at 30 June 2026 vs \u00a337.1m at 30 June 2025; CFR forecast to rise from \u00a392.2m (March 2026) to \u00a3180.4m (March 2027), against a \u00a3191m authorised limit \u2014 includes a \u00a310m 10-year PWLB EIP loan drawn 29 May 2026 at 4.95%","why":"Debt has more than doubled in a year and is planned to roughly double again within twelve months to finance a \u00a3189.6m capital programme, a very large build-out for a small district that narrows headroom under the statutory limit."}],"key_figures":[{"name":"gross borrowing","value":"\u00a390.466m gross external debt (30 June 2025: \u00a337.1m)","as_at":"2026-06-30","page":5},{"name":"cfr","value":"\u00a392.174m at 31 March 2026; estimated \u00a3180.359m at 31 March 2027 per 2026/27 TMSS","page":5},{"name":"authorised limit","value":"\u00a3191.000m for 2026/27 (not exceeded)","page":5},{"name":"operational boundary","value":"\u00a3186.000m for 2026/27","page":5},{"name":"investments","value":"\u00a344.406m, all maturities under one year (30 June 2025: \u00a328.451m)","as_at":"2026-06-30","page":6},{"name":"money market funds","value":"\u00a340.203m of the \u00a344.406m investment balance","as_at":"2026-06-30","page":7},{"name":"new pwlb loan","value":"\u00a310m 10-year EIP loan from PWLB drawn 29 May 2026 at 4.95% fixed (HRA concessionary rate)","page":2},{"name":"capital expenditure","value":"\u00a313.13