s":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-26","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-08","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Panel","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-10","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-08-25","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Panel","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed; Extraordinary","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-08-27","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Overview & Scrutiny Panel","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-09","committee":"Climate Change Cabinet Advisory Group","time":"2.30 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Cabinet","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://democracy.thanet.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"All figures in report are provisional pending publication of final Statements of Account","lead":"Audited accounts are authoritative; reported figures may change materially during the accounts process, affecting materiality of treasury position","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Housing Revenue Account borrowing now exceeds its financing requirement by \u00a33.7m for the first time","lead":"Overborrowing exceeds prudential borrowing limits and indicates timing mismatch between debt taken and capital spending; though mitigated by expected resolution","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Council shifted from net investment position of \u00a31.7m to net debt of \u00a348.3m","lead":"Net debt position reflects the council's overall cash strength and financial flexibility; deterioration indicates reduced headroom and increased reliance on borrowing","iso":"2026-09-24","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","headline":"All figures in report are provisional pending publication of final Statements of Account","detail":"The treasury management report presents year-end figures as provisional, noting that final Statements of Account for 2025/26 have not yet been published. The council indicates that members will be updated of any material changes that arise from the final accounts process.","category":"governance","matters":"Audited accounts are authoritative; reported figures may change materially during the accounts process, affecting materiality of treasury position","figures":"All 31 March 2026 balances are provisional","quote":"The Council has not yet published its final Statements of Account for 2025/26 so the figures in this report are subject to change. Members will be updated, at future meetings, of any material changes that arise.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","headline":"Housing Revenue Account borrowing now exceeds its financing requirement by \u00a33.7m for the first time","detail":"The HRA is now in an overborrowed position, with gross debt of \u00a355.0m exceeding the Capital Financing Requirement of \u00a351.3m. While the overall council shows underborrowing of \u00a311.2m (General Fund underborrowed by \u00a315.0m offset by HRA overborrowing of \u00a33.7m), the council's treasury strategy indicates this HRA overborrowing will be resolved within the next two financial years.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Overborrowing exceeds prudential borrowing limits and indicates timing mismatch between debt taken and capital spending; though mitigated by expected resolution","figures":"HRA debt \u00a355.009m vs CFR \u00a351.266m; HRA overborrowing \u00a33.7m; overall underborrowing \u00a311.247m (GF underborrowing \u00a315.0m, HRA overborrowing \u00a33.7m)","quote":"The overall CFR underfunding of \u00a311.3m is comprised of \u00a315.0m GF underfunding and \u00a3(3.7)m HRA overfunding. As per section 6.5.1 above, it is estimated that this HRA overfunding will be utilised within the next two financial years.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","headline":"Council shifted from net investment position of \u00a31.7m to net debt of \u00a348.3m","detail":"At 31 March 2025, the council had investments of \u00a335.4m exceeding debt of \u00a337.1m, creating a net investment position of \u00a31.7m. By 31 March 2026, with debt increased to \u00a380.9m and investments decreased to \u00a332.7m, the council was in a net debt position of \u00a348.3m. This represents a swing of approximately \u00a350m in the council's net cash position.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Net debt position reflects the council's overall cash strength and financial flexibility; deterioration indicates reduced headroom and increased reliance on borrowing","figures":"Net position shifted from \u00a31.746m net investment (March 2025) to \u00a348.254m net debt (March 2026); gross debt \u00a380.926m, investments \u00a332.672m","quote":"This table also shows that the Council's investments totalled \u00a332.672m at the 2025/26 year end and therefore was in a net debt position, as debt held exceeded investments by \u00a348.254m.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","headline":"Interest rates on new council borrowing increased from 4.16% to 4.97% between July 2025 and March 2026","detail":"The council took five PWLB loans during 2025/26, with rates rising from 4.16% in July to 4.97% in March. Gilt yields rose substantially through the year, with particularly steep increases in March 2026 due to inflation concerns related to the Middle East conflict. This resulted in higher borrowing costs than might have been expected earlier in the financial year.","category":"borrowing","matters":"Rising cost of capital increases council service costs and reduces affordability of future borrowing; indicates a challenging market environment","figures":"Five loans at 4.16%, 4.41%, 4.53%, 4.58%, 4.97% between 09/07/25 and 26/03/26","quote":"Gilt yields have been volatile through 2025/26. The low point for long-term rates of 25 and 50 years duration was reached early in April 2025 whilst the low points for short and medium dated rates were reached in early 2026, prior to the outbreak of the Middle East conflict.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-24","committee":"Council","paper_title":"Council Treasury YE 25-26","paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97583/97583.pdf","headline":"Capital expenditure was \u00a359.0m against a budget of \u00a3159.6m, delivering only 37% of planned investment","detail":"The council budgeted \u00a3159.6m of capital expenditure for 2025/26 but delivered only \u00a359.0m, representing a 63% underspend. This comprised General Fund \u00a329.8m against budget \u00a379.6m and HRA \u00a329.2m against budget \u00a380.0m. The council has acknowledged significant slippage in the capital programme as an issue requiring action.","category":"capital","matters":"Major capital programme underspend suggests project management or delivery constraints; indicates capital assets and improvements are being delayed","figures":"\u00a3159.6m budgeted, \u00a359.0m actual; General Fund \u00a379.6m budget vs \u00a329.8m actual; HRA \u00a380.0m budget vs \u00a329.2m actual","quote":"Slippage will not be an acceptable norm. Capital schemes will be at risk of having their Council funding re-directed should there be delays that cannot be substantiated (schemes that are externally funded may require more flexibility however).","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-08-27"},"name":"Thanet","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-20","since_iso":"2026-08-21","distress":false,"headline":"Waste service overspending by \u00a3188,000","lead":"Operational overspends in a core waste service indicate budget control or demand management issues, which affects the council's financial sustainability and controls","also":["18 other findings in this window","6 papers caught"],"watch":"Overview & Scrutiny Panel on 2026-10-20","n_findings":19,"n_documents":6,"top_paper_title":"Annex 4 - Sheet1","top_paper_url":"https://thanet.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s97227/97227.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":107,"news_drafts_total":3}}